# The Forge — Content Guidelines

Official source (always prefer current text over this summary):

- [Content Guidelines](https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/content-guidelines)
- [File structure](https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/content-guidelines#file-structure)

When packaging, releasing, documenting install paths, or publishing/updating mods on The Forge, follow these rules.

## File structure (critical)

Archives must be **installation-ready**: extract into the SPT **game root** with no extra wrapping folder and no manual path fixes.

Use `.zip` or `.7z` only. No password protection. Include everything needed to run.

### SPT 4.x layout in the archive root

Server mod:

```text
SPT/user/mods/<ModFolder>/
  <Mod>.dll
  config.json   # if used
```

Client mod (BepInEx):

```text
BepInEx/plugins/<Plugin>.dll
# or BepInEx/plugins/<PluginFolder>/...
```

Client + server combo: both trees at archive root (`SPT/...` and `BepInEx/...`).

### Wrong (do not ship)

```text
user/mods/<ModFolder>/          # missing SPT/ prefix on SPT 4
SPT/BepInEx/plugins/...         # BepInEx must not be nested under SPT/
MyMod-1.0.0/SPT/user/mods/...   # extra top-level wrapper folder
```

Local `Build/` output should match the archive layout. Zip from that layout (`SPT`, `BepInEx`, or both) — do not zip only the inner `user/` tree.

Install docs must describe the same paths (`SPT/user/mods/...`, `BepInEx/plugins/...`).

## Publishing checklist (Forge)

- SemVer; client/server versions must match; SPT constraint (`~4.0.13`, `~4.0.0`, etc.) must match testing
- Source link required for client/server binaries; VirusTotal link per release archive
- Descriptions: step-by-step install + basic config/usage; declare dependencies on the version
- Client `[BepInPlugin]`: GUID matches Forge + server; name `Username-ModName`; SemVer matches
- Server C# (4.0+): `ModGuid` / `Version` / `SptVersion` consistent with Forge and client
- **No mod packs / compilations** on Forge; do not redistribute others’ mods or assets without permission
- Link only your own mod source/releases — not a pack repo or installer that bundles third-party work
- Direct download links only (e.g. GitHub Releases `.zip`/`.7z`)
- No watermark changes; no obfuscation; no unauthorized network/telemetry
- AI: do not ship substantially AI-written mods; if any LLM assistance was used, set “Contains AI Content”

Target platform for new work: **SPT 4.0.13** (see `spt-version.mdc`).
